Mark XXIV: the Bridge streams

The phone showed only final replies; the browser has streamed since
Mark XXIII. Parity, via the same proven machinery.

- serve.py: the bridge turn worker passes on_text_delta to the agent and
  pushes throttled "partial" events (0.4s interval, one final partial
  before the reply) - identical pattern to the dashboard. MAX_EVENTS
  600 -> 1200.
- serve_page.py: the bridge panel renders partials in a growing bubble
  with a caret, replaced by the final reply event; the user bubble
  clears any stale stream.
- Tests: the bridge confirm/deny fakes now implement create_chat_stream
  (the agent has no create_chat fallback on the streaming path - Mark
  XXIII lesson); new bridge streaming round-trip with FakeStreamChain -
  partials arrive, grow monotonically, final reply matches.
- Version 3.11.0.
